<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line">
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document">Market-Based Data Subset Selection - Principled Aggregation of Multi-Criteria Example Utility</h1>
<div class="ltx_authors">
<span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Ashish Jha
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span><span id="id1" class="ltx_text">Skolkovo Institute of Science and Technology</span>
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_email"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Email: </span><a href="mailto:"><span id="id2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">ashish.jha@skoltech.ru</span></a>
</span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Valentin Leplat
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span><span id="id3" class="ltx_text">Innopolis University</span>
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_email"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Email: </span><a href="mailto:"><span id="id4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">v.leplat@innopolis.ru</span></a>
</span></span></span></span>
<span class="ltx_author_before">  </span><span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Anh Huy Phan
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span><span id="id5" class="ltx_text">Skolkovo Institute of Science and Technology</span>
</span>
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_email"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Email: </span><a href="mailto:"><span id="id6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">a.phan@skoltech.ru</span></a>
</span></span></span></span></div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="abstract1.1.1" class="ltx_text">Selecting a small yet useful subset of training data is hard because signals of example utility (uncertainty, rarity, diversity, etc.) are heterogeneous and typically combined with ad hoc weights. We propose a market-based selector that prices each example via a cost-function prediction market (LMSR), signals act as traders, a single liquidity parameter controls concentration, and topic-wise normalization stabilizes calibration. Token budgets are handled explicitly by a price-per-token rule <math id="abstract1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=p/\ell^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>γ</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=p/\ell^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="abstract1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> exposing an interpretable length bias; a lightweight diversity head improves coverage. We quantify coverage via topic cluster coverage and effective sample size. On the theory side, we show that LMSR implements a maximum-entropy aggregation with exponential weighting and a convex objective, yielding transparent knobs for aggregation strength. Empirically, on GSM8K (60k-token budget) the market with diversity achieves parity with strong single-signal baselines while reducing seed variance and incurring <math id="abstract1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="&lt;\!0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>0.1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">&lt;\!0.1</annotation></semantics></math> GPU-hr selection overhead; on AGNews at kept=5-25% the market (with light balancing) delivers competitive accuracy with improved balance and stability. The framework unifies multi-signal data curation under fixed compute for prompt-level reasoning and classification.</span></p>
  
</div>
<div id="p1" class="ltx_para">
<table id="p1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_top">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="p1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:0.0pt;height:24.0pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"></span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">1 </span>Introduction</h2>

<figure id="S1.F1" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.02456v1/Diagrams.svg" id="S1.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:505/113;" width="505" height="113"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span><span id="S1.F1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Overview.</span> Signals (uncertainty, rarity, diversity) are standardized within topic and
aggregated by a topic-separable LMSR with liquidity <math id="S1.F1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> to produce prices. Selection is either
balanced top-<math id="S1.F1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> with per-topic floors or token-budgeted greedy by <math id="S1.F1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}=p_{i}/\ell_{i}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi>i</mi><mi>γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}=p_{i}/\ell_{i}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math>.
We apply this to prompt-level reasoning; model training shows standard fine-tuning, with LoRA adapters
included illustratively only <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hu et al., 2021</a>)</cite>.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Training on ever-larger datasets is costly, and many examples contribute little to the final accuracy
previous work suggests that a large fraction can be removed with only minor degradation
<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Toneva et al., 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Paul et al., 2021</a>)</cite>.
<span id="S1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
This motivates data subset selection under a fixed
compute (token) budget. The difficulty is that example utility is intrinsically multi–faceted
uncertainty, distributional rarity, and diversity often disagree and most existing methods either
optimize a single facet (e.g., uncertainty sampling <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Settles, 2009a</a>)</cite>) or combine signals with
hand-tuned weights that are brittle across tasks. This problem is amplified in instruction tuning and
prompt–level reasoning, where items have highly variable lengths and redundancies. A selector must
therefore be token-aware, reward informative prompts, avoid duplicates, and remain stable across
random seeds without heavy tuning. The growing importance of data curation for LLMs makes this
question practically urgent: large-scale instruction datasets (e.g., GSM8K) contain millions
of tokens, and small improvements in selection can translate directly to reduced compute costs and
improved downstream robustness.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We cast <em id="S1.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">data selection as a tiny prediction market</em> where each training item is a “contract” and its <em id="S1.p2.1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">price</em> reflects how useful it is to train on. Several simple <em id="S1.p2.1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">bots</em> (signals) e.g., uncertainty (mean token-level NLL), embedding-space rarity (<math id="S1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-NN), and an optional diversity score each examine every item and emit a standardized value <em id="S1.p2.1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">within its topic</em> so heterogeneous groups remain comparable. We then: (i) <em id="S1.p2.1.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">standardize</em> signals within topic, (ii) <em id="S1.p2.1.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">add</em> them into a single share per item,</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}\;=\;\sum_{m=1}^{M}w_{m}\,\tilde{s}_{i}^{(m)}\quad\text{(topic-wise $z$-scores $\tilde{s}$)}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.558em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.391em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(topic-wise </mtext><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">-scores </mtext><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mtext></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}\;=\;\sum_{m=1}^{M}w_{m}\,\tilde{s}_{i}^{(m)}\quad\text{(topic-wise $z$-scores $\tilde{s}$)},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(iii) convert shares to <em id="S1.p2.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">prices</em> with a <em id="S1.p2.2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">topic-separable LMSR</em> (cost-function market) for topic budgets <math id="S1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and liquidities <math id="S1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}=\alpha_{t(i)}\Big[\mathrm{softmax}_{I_{t(i)}}\!\big(q/\beta_{t(i)}\big)\Big]_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">softmax</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}=\alpha_{t(i)}\Big[\mathrm{softmax}_{I_{t(i)}}\!\big(q/\beta_{t(i)}\big)\Big]_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">So larger <math id="S1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> smooths and smaller <math id="S1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> concentrates, and (iv) make selection <em id="S1.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">token-aware</em> by ranking items with <em id="S1.p3.1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">price-per-token</em></span></p>
<table id="S1.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S1.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}\;=\;\frac{p_{i}}{\ell_{i}^{\gamma}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.558em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}\;=\;\frac{p_{i}}{\ell_{i}^{\gamma}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S1.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">then greedily filling a fixed <em id="S1.p3.2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">token budget</em> <math id="S1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> (or using balanced top-<math id="S1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> with topic floors); here <math id="S1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is item length and <math id="S1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\!\geq\!0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.108em" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\!\geq\!0</annotation></semantics></math> is an explicit <em id="S1.p3.2.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">length-bias</em> knob (favor many short vs. fewer long items). This market view yields a <em id="S1.p3.2.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">principled, convex aggregation</em> (log-linear/exponential family) with a <em id="S1.p3.2.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">maximum-entropy</em> interpretation (we pick the least-committal distribution consistent with the signals), is <em id="S1.p3.2.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">topic-aware</em> by construction via <math id="S1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, and is <em id="S1.p3.2.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">efficient</em> (one pass for embeddings + signals; the only heavy step is optional <math id="S1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-NN via an <em id="S1.p3.2.1.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Approximate Nearest Neighbor (ANN)</em> index). In short, multiple weak, heterogeneous signals <math id="S1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math> one coherent probability per item via LMSR (not hand-tuned sums), then <em id="S1.p3.2.1.8" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">budget-aware</em> picking with a few interpretable knobs <math id="S1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\beta_{t},w_{m},\alpha_{t},\gamma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\beta_{t},w_{m},\alpha_{t},\gamma)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">2 </span>Problem formulation and method</h2>

<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.1 </span>Subset selection as market pricing</h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let </span><math id="S2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{(x_{i},y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{(x_{i},y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and let </span><math id="S2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}\subseteq\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒮</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊆</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}\subseteq\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> be a small training subset. We cast selection as pricing in a cost-function prediction market where each example </span><math id="S2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is a contract with price </span><math id="S2.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> reflecting utility for training. The Logarithmic Market Scoring Rule (LMSR) defines a convex cost</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(q)=\beta\log\!\Big(\sum_{j=1}^{N}e^{\,q_{j}/\beta}\Big),\ \beta&gt;0,\qquad p_{i}(q)=\frac{\partial C}{\partial q_{i}}=\frac{e^{\,q_{i}/\beta}}{\sum_{j}e^{\,q_{j}/\beta}}=\mathrm{softmax}(q/\beta)_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></munderover><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∂</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∂</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">softmax</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(q)=\beta\log\!\Big(\sum_{j=1}^{N}e^{\,q_{j}/\beta}\Big),\ \beta&gt;0,\qquad p_{i}(q)=\frac{\partial C}{\partial q_{i}}=\frac{e^{\,q_{i}/\beta}}{\sum_{j}e^{\,q_{j}/\beta}}=\mathrm{softmax}(q/\beta)_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">with outstanding shares </span><math id="S2.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in\mathbb{R}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in\mathbb{R}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and liquidity </span><math id="S2.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Prices are the gradient</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E1"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C(q)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\beta\log\!\Big(\sum_{j=1}^{N}e^{\,q_{j}/\beta}\Big),\qquad\beta&gt;0," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></munderover></mstyle><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\beta\log\!\Big(\sum_{j=1}^{N}e^{\,q_{j}/\beta}\Big),\qquad\beta&gt;0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p_{i}(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p_{i}(q)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\partial C}{\partial q_{i}}=\frac{e^{\,q_{i}/\beta}}{\sum_{j=1}^{N}e^{\,q_{j}/\beta}}=\big[\mathrm{softmax}(q/\beta)\big]_{i}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∂</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∂</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></msubsup><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\partial C}{\partial q_{i}}=\frac{e^{\,q_{i}/\beta}}{\sum_{j=1}^{N}e^{\,q_{j}/\beta}}=\big[\mathrm{softmax}(q/\beta)\big]_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, hence </span><math id="S2.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in\Delta^{N-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in\Delta^{N-1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is a probability distribution over examples. Cost-function markets and LMSR have a rich theory linking convex costs, proper scoring, and no-regret dynamics </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S2.SS1.p1.3.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hanson, 2007</a>; <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Abernethy et al., 2013</a>; <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen &amp; Vaughan, 2010</a>; <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lambert et al., 2008</a><span id="S2.SS1.p1.3.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S2.SS1.p1.3.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F2" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.02456v1/LSMR_mech.svg" id="S2.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:329/153;" width="329" height="153"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span><span id="S2.F2.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LMSR aggregation.</span> Prices <math id="S2.F2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\beta}(q)=\mathrm{softmax}(q/\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\beta}(q)=\mathrm{softmax}(q/\beta)</annotation></semantics></math> become smoother as <math id="S2.F2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> increases and more concentrated as <math id="S2.F2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> decreases.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Intuitively, LMSR behaves like a temperature-controlled softmax, prices concentrate as liquidity </span><math id="S2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> decreases and smooth as </span><math id="S2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> increases. See Fig. </span><a href="#S2.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 2.1 Subset selection as market pricing ‣ 2 Problem formulation and method ‣ Market-Based Data Subset Selection - Principled Aggregation of Multi-Criteria Example Utility" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a><span id="S2.SS1.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for the price curves and Fig. </span><a href="#S2.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ 2.1 Subset selection as market pricing ‣ 2 Problem formulation and method ‣ Market-Based Data Subset Selection - Principled Aggregation of Multi-Criteria Example Utility" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a><span id="S2.SS1.p2.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for entropy </span><math id="S2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(\mathbf{p})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐩</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(\mathbf{p})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p2.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> versus </span><math id="S2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS1.p2.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. This temperature view also underpins the market-maker’s convexity guarantees</span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S2.SS1.p2.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hanson, 2007</a>; <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Abernethy et al., 2013</a><span id="S2.SS1.p2.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S2.SS1.p2.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S2.F3" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.02456v1/figure2_lmsr_aggregation.png" id="S2.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:329/105;" width="329" height="105" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span><span id="S2.F3.17" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Effect of liquidity on aggregation.</span>
<em id="S2.F3.18" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Left:</em> mixed two-dimensional proxy signals and the blended score
<math id="S2.F3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=0.55\,u_{z}+0.30\,d_{z}+0.15\,r_{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.55</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">u</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.30</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.15</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=0.55\,u_{z}+0.30\,d_{z}+0.15\,r_{z}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<em id="S2.F3.19" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Middle:</em> topic-separable LMSR prices <math id="S2.F3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=\mathrm{softmax}(S/\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\mathrm{softmax}(S/\beta)</annotation></semantics></math> for two liquidities
(lower <math id="S2.F3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> concentrates mass, higher <math id="S2.F3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> smooths).
<em id="S2.F3.20" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Right:</em> price entropy <math id="S2.F3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(p)</annotation></semantics></math> versus <math id="S2.F3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math> (entropy increases with liquidity).</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.2 </span>Aggregating heterogeneous signals</h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Example utility is multi-faceted. We expose complementary signals such as token-level NLL (uncertainty), </span><math id="S2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">NN anti-density in embedding space (rarity), and a lightweight diversity score; optional signals like grad-norm can be included when available. Each signal is standardized within topic, and bots contribute linearly through shares </span><math id="S2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q=\sum_{m}w_{m}\,\tilde{s}^{(m)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q=\sum_{m}w_{m}\,\tilde{s}^{(m)}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> with nonnegative weights </span><math id="S2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{m}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, after which prices follow by </span><math id="S2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=\mathrm{softmax}(q/\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\mathrm{softmax}(q/\beta)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
Our convention follows the LMSR cost </span><math id="S2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(q)=\beta\log\sum_{j}e^{q_{j}/\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(q)=\beta\log\sum_{j}e^{q_{j}/\beta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, whose gradient yields the price vector </span><math id="S2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=\nabla C(q)=\text{softmax}(q/\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\nabla C(q)=\text{softmax}(q/\beta)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Here </span><math id="S2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> controls the liquidity/temperature of the market. The weights control the relative contribution of the signals, and the single parameter </span><math id="S2.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS2.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> globally controls concentration versus smoothing.</span></p>
<table id="S2.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}=\sum_{m}w_{m}\tilde{s}^{(m)}_{i},\qquad p_{i}=\mathrm{softmax}\!\big(q/\beta\big)_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:3.720em;" width="3.720em"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">softmax</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}=\sum_{m}w_{m}\tilde{s}^{(m)}_{i},\qquad p_{i}=\mathrm{softmax}\!\big(q/\beta\big)_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">When desired, we tune </span><math id="S2.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS2.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> via a single pass of multiplicative-weights/EG on a tiny dev split </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S2.SS2.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Arora et al., 2012</a><span id="S2.SS2.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S2.SS2.p1.2.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Unless stated, we use equal weights </span><math id="S2.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{m}=1/M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{m}=1/M</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS2.p1.2.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. On a tiny dev split we optionally
tune </span><math id="S2.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{m}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS2.p1.2.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> via a Hedge/Exponentiated-Gradient (EG) update over a small grid.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Standardization is performed within topic </span><math id="S2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Let </span><math id="S2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t(i)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> denote the topic of example </span><math id="S2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
Then</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{s}_{i}^{(m)}\;=\;\frac{s_{i}^{(m)}-\mu_{t(i)}^{(m)}}{\sigma_{t(i)}^{(m)}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.558em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{s}_{i}^{(m)}\;=\;\frac{s_{i}^{(m)}-\mu_{t(i)}^{(m)}}{\sigma_{t(i)}^{(m)}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">with rank-to-</span><math id="S2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS2.p2.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> normalization applied when the distribution is heavy-tailed.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.3 </span>Budgeted decision and implementation</h3>

<div id="S2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Selection is token-aware - For token cost </span><math id="S2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> we rank by the price-per-token score </span><math id="S2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}=p_{i}/\ell_{i}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}=p_{i}/\ell_{i}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and greedily add examples while respecting a total budget </span><math id="S2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> tokens; the exponent </span><math id="S2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is an interpretable length bias. When rate constraints are preferred, a balanced top-</span><math id="S2.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> variant allocates minimum per-topic floors before filling the remaining slots by global price, and stochastic sampling from </span><math id="S2.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> offers a soft exploration mode if desired. In practice, we make a single pass to extract frozen embeddings, compute signals (ANN indices for </span><math id="S2.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">NN), standardize within topic, mix into shares, price with LMSR, and select by the budgeted rule. Pricing itself is </span><math id="S2.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">; the only super-linear component is optional approximate </span><math id="S2.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">NN construction. We use ANN indices for diversity/rarity queries (FAISS, HNSW) </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Johnson et al., 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Malkov &amp; Yashunin, 2020</a><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. In experiments we use </span><math id="S2.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in\{1.4,1.6,1.8\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1.4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1.6</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1.8</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in\{1.4,1.6,1.8\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> with </span><math id="S2.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=1.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=1.6</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.16" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> as the default.
When optimizing a monotone submodular coverage surrogate </span><math id="S2.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\mathcal{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒮</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\mathcal{S})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.17" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (e.g., facility-location or
budgeted maximum coverage) under a knapsack budget, there exist algorithms with </span><math id="S2.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-1/e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-1/e)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.18" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-type
guarantees </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.19" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nemhauser et al., 1978</a>; <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Khuller et al., 1999</a>; <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sviridenko, 2004</a><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.21" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.22" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
Our default selector ranks by </span><math id="S2.SS3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}=p_{i}/\ell_{i}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}=p_{i}/\ell_{i}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.23" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and maximizes the </span><em id="S2.SS3.p1.1.24" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">modular</em><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.25" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> score
</span><math id="S2.SS3.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\in\mathcal{S}}p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\in\mathcal{S}}p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.26" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">; this density-greedy rule is a practical heuristic but does </span><em id="S2.SS3.p1.1.27" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">not</em><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.28" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> carry
a </span><math id="S2.SS3.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-1/e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-1/e)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS3.p1.1.29" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> guarantee.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">2.4 </span>Topic-separable markets for prompts</h3>

<div id="S2.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">To prevent any topic from dominating, we use a topic-separable LMSR. With topic index </span><math id="S2.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t(i)\in\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t(i)\in\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, partitions </span><math id="S2.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℐ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, budgets </span><math id="S2.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> with </span><math id="S2.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t}\alpha_{t}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t}\alpha_{t}=1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and per-topic liquidity </span><math id="S2.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">,</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S2.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(q)=\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\alpha_{t}\,\beta_{t}\log\!\Big(\sum_{j\in I_{t}}e^{\,q_{j}/\beta_{t}}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒯</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(q)=\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\alpha_{t}\,\beta_{t}\log\!\Big(\sum_{j\in I_{t}}e^{\,q_{j}/\beta_{t}}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Prices are</span></p>
<table id="S2.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}=\alpha_{t(i)}\Big[\mathrm{softmax}_{I_{t(i)}}\!\big(q/\beta_{t(i)}\big)\Big]_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">softmax</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}=\alpha_{t(i)}\Big[\mathrm{softmax}_{I_{t(i)}}\!\big(q/\beta_{t(i)}\big)\Big]_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2.5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">As </span><math id="S2.SS4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="S2.SS4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(q)\to\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\alpha_{t}\max_{j\in I_{t}}q_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒯</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">max</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(q)\to\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\alpha_{t}\max_{j\in I_{t}}q_{j}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">;
as </span><math id="S2.SS4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, prices become uniform within topic </span><math id="S2.SS4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.p4.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S2.SS4.p4.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Abernethy et al., 2013</a>; <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen &amp; Vaughan, 2010</a><span id="S2.SS4.p4.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S2.SS4.p4.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Market-Based Subset Selection (Topic-Separable LMSR, Budgeted Greedy)</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Dataset </span><math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">; topics </span><math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t(i)\!\in\!\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.108em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t(i)\!\in\!\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> with partitions </span><math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{I_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{I_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">; signals </span><math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\phi^{(k)}\}_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\phi^{(k)}\}_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">; token budget </span><math id="alg1.l1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">; topic budgets </span><math id="alg1.l1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\alpha_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\alpha_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (</span><math id="alg1.l1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t}\alpha_{t}\!=\!1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t}\alpha_{t}\!=\!1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">); liquidities </span><math id="alg1.l1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\beta_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\beta_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">; length-bias </span><math id="alg1.l1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\text{len}}\!\geq\!0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">len</mtext></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.108em" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\text{len}}\!\geq\!0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Subset </span><math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}\subseteq\{1,\dots,n\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℛ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊆</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}\subseteq\{1,\dots,n\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> with </span><math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\in\mathcal{R}}\ell_{i}\leq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℛ</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\in\mathcal{R}}\ell_{i}\leq B</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l2.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Defaults:</span><span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}\!=\!1/K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.108em" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}\!=\!1/K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l3.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="alg1.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}\!\propto\!|I_{t}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.108em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.108em">∝</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}\!\propto\!|I_{t}|</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l3.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="alg1.l3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}\!=\!\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.108em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.108em">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}\!=\!\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l3.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">; precompute token lengths </span><math id="alg1.l3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l3.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Signals &amp; standardization:</span><span id="alg1.l4.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S^{(k)}\!\leftarrow\!\text{Normalize}_{t}\!\big(\phi^{(k)}(x_{i};\theta)\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.108em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.108em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Normalize</mtext><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">θ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S^{(k)}\!\leftarrow\!\text{Normalize}_{t}\!\big(\phi^{(k)}(x_{i};\theta)\big)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l4.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for all </span><math id="alg1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l4.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (topic-wise)
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Shares:</span><span id="alg1.l5.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}\leftarrow\sum_{k=1}^{K}w_{k}\,S^{(k)}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}\leftarrow\sum_{k=1}^{K}w_{k}\,S^{(k)}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l5.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Pricing (per topic):</span><span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{I_{t}}\leftarrow\alpha_{t}\cdot\mathrm{softmax}_{I_{t}}\!\big(q_{I_{t}}/\beta_{t}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">softmax</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{I_{t}}\leftarrow\alpha_{t}\cdot\mathrm{softmax}_{I_{t}}\!\big(q_{I_{t}}/\beta_{t}\big)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l6.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for all </span><math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathcal{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒯</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathcal{T}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l6.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Price-per-token:</span><span id="alg1.l7.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}\leftarrow p_{i}/\ell_{i}^{\gamma_{\text{len}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">len</mtext></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}\leftarrow p_{i}/\ell_{i}^{\gamma_{\text{len}}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l7.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">  for all </span><math id="alg1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l7.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Budgeted greedy:</span><span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}\leftarrow\mathrm{GreedySelect}(\rho,\ell,B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℛ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">GreedySelect</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}\leftarrow\mathrm{GreedySelect}(\rho,\ell,B)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l8.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><span id="alg1.l8.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;float:right;"><math id="alg1.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> scan items by <math id="alg1.l8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>; add if fits
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l9.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">return</span><span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="alg1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℛ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="alg1.l9.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="S2.SS4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS4.p5.1" class="ltx_p">
<span id="S2.SS4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="width:397.5pt;">
<span id="S2.SS4.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.p5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Practitioner defaults.</span><span id="S2.SS4.p5.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Set </span><math id="S2.SS4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta{=}2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta{=}2</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.p5.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="S2.SS4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma{=}1.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma{=}1.6</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.p5.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="S2.SS4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}{=}1/K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}{=}1/K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.p5.1.1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and </span><math id="S2.SS4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}\propto|I_{t}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∝</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}\propto|I_{t}|</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.p5.1.1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">; for ANN we use FAISS/HNSW </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S2.SS4.p5.1.1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Johnson et al., 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Malkov &amp; Yashunin, 2020</a><span id="S2.SS4.p5.1.1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S2.SS4.p5.1.1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></span>
</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Notes.</span><span id="S2.SS4.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Signals are standardized within topic and mixed into shares
</span><math id="S2.SS4.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}=\sum_{k}w_{k}\,\tilde{s}^{(k)}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}=\sum_{k}w_{k}\,\tilde{s}^{(k)}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.p6.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">; prices are topic-separable
</span><math id="S2.SS4.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{I_{t}}=\alpha_{t}\,\mathrm{softmax}_{I_{t}}(q_{I_{t}}/\beta_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">softmax</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{I_{t}}=\alpha_{t}\,\mathrm{softmax}_{I_{t}}(q_{I_{t}}/\beta_{t})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.p6.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
Selection uses the price-per-token score </span><math id="S2.SS4.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}=p_{i}/\ell_{i}^{\gamma_{\text{len}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">len</mtext></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}=p_{i}/\ell_{i}^{\gamma_{\text{len}}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.p6.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and a greedy
pack under the token budget </span><math id="S2.SS4.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.p6.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">; minimal per-topic floors can be applied before greedy to ensure
coverage. Unless noted: </span><math id="S2.SS4.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}{=}1/K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}{=}1/K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.p6.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="S2.SS4.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}\propto|I_{t}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∝</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}\propto|I_{t}|</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.p6.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and </span><math id="S2.SS4.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}{=}\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}{=}\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.p6.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. The selector is </span><math id="S2.SS4.p6.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(NK)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(NK)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.p6.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for scoring/pricing (excluding optional ANN for kNN); see §§2.2–2.4 for details.</span></p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Scalability and complexity.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Signal computation and pricing are linear in the pool size and number of signals, </span><math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(NK)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(NK)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
for standardization and mixing, plus </span><math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for LMSR pricing. The optional diversity head
is dominated by kNN; with an ANN index (e.g., HNSW/FAISS) the build is </span><math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N\log N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N\log N)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and
queries are sublinear in practice. Memory is </span><math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(Nd)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(Nd)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for </span><math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-dimensional embeddings plus
</span><math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for prices and shares; all steps are streamable. The greedy pack is </span><math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N\log N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N\log N)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for a single sort
(by </span><math id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S2.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) and a linear scan to admit items under the token budget. In our runs the end-to-end
selection overhead (signals+pricing) is negligible relative to fine-tuning (see §5.1).</span></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">3 </span>Theoretical analysis</h2>

<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.1 </span>Maximum-entropy view</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposition 1 (Entropic aggregation).</span><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Let </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s^{(m)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s^{(m)}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> be signal functions and </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in\Delta^{N-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in\Delta^{N-1}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> market prices. The solution of</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{p\in\Delta^{N-1}}H(p)\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\mathbb{E}_{p}[s^{(m)}]=\bar{s}^{(m)}\ \ \forall m" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><munder><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">max</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s.t.</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{p\in\Delta^{N-1}}H(p)\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\mathbb{E}_{p}[s^{(m)}]=\bar{s}^{(m)}\ \ \forall m</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">has the Gibbs form </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}^{\star}\propto\exp(\sum_{m}\lambda_{m}s_{i}^{(m)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⋆</mo></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∝</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}^{\star}\propto\exp(\sum_{m}\lambda_{m}s_{i}^{(m)})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">; setting </span><math id="S3.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{m}=\beta w_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{m}=\beta w_{m}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS1.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> recovers LMSR prices. </span>
<br class="ltx_break"><em id="S3.SS1.p1.2.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Sketch of the proof.</em><span id="S3.SS1.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Lagrange multipliers on linear moment constraints yield an exponential family; LMSR implements its gradient map.The resulting Gibbs form also admits a multiplicative-weights interpretation of the Lagrange multipliers </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S3.SS1.p1.2.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Arora et al., 2012</a><span id="S3.SS1.p1.2.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S3.SS1.p1.2.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Utility recovery under noisy signals</h3>

<section id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposition 2 (Recovery with weak but monotone signals).</h4>

<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let </span><math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U\in[0,1]^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U\in[0,1]^{N}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> be unknown utilities and suppose the aggregated score
</span><math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S=\sum_{m}w_{m}\,\tilde{s}^{(m)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S=\sum_{m}w_{m}\,\tilde{s}^{(m)}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is monotone in </span><math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> in expectation and sub-Gaussian with
signal-to-noise ratio at least </span><math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Let </span><math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> denote prices computed with liquidity </span><math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
Then selecting the top-</span><math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> by </span><math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> attains utility at least </span><math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\varepsilon)\,\mathrm{OPT}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">OPT</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\varepsilon)\,\mathrm{OPT}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> with
probability at least </span><math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, where</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon=O\!\left(\sigma\sqrt{\frac{\log(N/\delta)}{K\,\Gamma^{2}}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ε</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon=O\!\left(\sigma\sqrt{\frac{\log(N/\delta)}{K\,\Gamma^{2}}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<br class="ltx_break">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><em id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Sketch of the proof.</em><span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Exponential weighting amplifies aligned signal and averages independent noise; standard concentration yields the bound. </span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Discussion.</span><span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> The guarantee highlights that exponential weighting acts like a form of
signal amplification, weak but aligned signals are boosted while independent noise is averaged out,
similar in spirit to boosting and multiplicative weights. The </span><math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(\sqrt{\log(N/\delta)}/(K\gamma^{2}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(\sqrt{\log(N/\delta)}/(K\gamma^{2}))</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">
dependence emphasizes that more examples and stronger alignment reduce the gap to the optimum.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Intuition.</span><span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> LMSR can be viewed as a temperature-controlled aggregator - with small
liquidity, only the strongest signals dominate, while with large liquidity, all signals contribute
nearly uniformly. This explains why tuning </span><math id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is sufficient to interpolate between “winner-take-all”
and “average-everything” regimes. Such convex interpolation is not available to ad hoc weighted sums.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Diversity and coverage</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proposition 3 (Coverage with a diversity head).</span><span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> If a diversity signal based on centroid distance or </span><math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">NN anti-density receives positive weight, the selected set preserves a constant fraction of embedding variance and admits a covering radius </span><math id="S3.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=O(\sqrt{d\log(N/\delta)/K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=O(\sqrt{d\log(N/\delta)/K})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> with probability </span><math id="S3.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span>
<br class="ltx_break"><span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Discussion.</span><span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> This result connects the diversity head to classic covering number and
</span><math id="S3.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-center bounds, by ensuring a non-zero weight on anti-density, the selected set achieves a radius
comparable to facility-location objectives. This provides theoretical backing for the empirical
coverage gains seen in our ablations.This connects empirically used facility-location style objectives to our market signal with a diversity head </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wei et al., 2015</a>; <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lin &amp; Bilmes, 2011</a><span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S3.SS3.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.4 </span>Prompt-specific trading signals</h3>

<div id="S3.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Each bot emits a scalar score per item and the market aggregates via </span><math id="S3.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}=\sum_{m}w_{m}\,\tilde{s}_{i}^{(m)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}=\sum_{m}w_{m}\,\tilde{s}_{i}^{(m)}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> as in Eq. </span><a href="#S2.E3" title="In 2.2 Aggregating heterogeneous signals ‣ 2 Problem formulation and method ‣ Market-Based Data Subset Selection - Principled Aggregation of Multi-Criteria Example Utility" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a><span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, with standardization performed </span><em id="S3.SS4.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">within topic</em><span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and, for length-sensitive quantities, per token. For instruction tuning, difficulty is the mean token-level NLL (or perplexity) of the reference response under a base/teacher LM; We pair standard uncertainty cues from active learning with Bayesian approximations </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib25" title="" class="ltx_ref">Settles, 2009b</a>; <a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lewis &amp; Gale, 1994</a>; <a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gal &amp; Ghahramani, 2016</a>; <a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Houlsby et al., 2011</a>; <a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kirsch et al., 2019</a><span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, for chain-of-thought we average a few stochastic decodes to obtain a self-consistency dispersion signal. For code and math, correctness proxies score the next-token distribution restricted to answer formats (e.g., boxed numerals or unit-tested stubs), optionally augmented with an execution success bit when tests exist. Diversity is computed in an instruction-embedding space </span><math id="S3.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(p_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(p_{i})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (sentence encoders), combining centroid distance with a </span><math id="S3.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">NN anti-density radius so isolated prompts receive higher bids; rarity is defined topic-wise to counter over-represented templates; robustness is estimated by paraphrase invariance via the variance of LM/reward scores over neutral rewrites </span><math id="S3.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta(p_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta(p_{i})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, bidding up semantically stable prompts. Alignment/safety enter as calibrated scores on </span><math id="S3.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{i},r_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{i},r_{i})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, with high-risk pairs down-weighted and borderline but educational pairs lightly positive and then topic-normalized. All raw signals </span><math id="S3.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}^{(m)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}^{(m)}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> are </span><math id="S3.SS4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-scored inside </span><math id="S3.SS4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{I}_{t(i)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℐ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{I}_{t(i)}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.16" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and, when appropriate, divided by </span><math id="S3.SS4.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sqrt{\ell_{i}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></msqrt><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sqrt{\ell_{i}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS4.p1.1.17" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to equalize per-token evidence before mixing.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.5 </span>Token-budgeted selection and prompt packs</h3>

<div id="S3.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">LLM training and prompting operate under a token budget, given prices </span><math id="S3.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and costs </span><math id="S3.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}=\ell_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}=\ell_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, we choose </span><math id="S3.SS5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{S}\subseteq\{1,\dots,N\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒮</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊆</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{S}\subseteq\{1,\dots,N\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> that maximizes </span><math id="S3.SS5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\in\mathcal{S}}p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\in\mathcal{S}}p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> subject to </span><math id="S3.SS5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\in\mathcal{S}}c_{i}\leq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\in\mathcal{S}}c_{i}\leq B</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. A practical selector ranks by the price-per-token score </span><math id="S3.SS5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}=p_{i}/c_{i}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}=p_{i}/c_{i}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and greedily adds items while respecting </span><math id="S3.SS5.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, with small topic-wise floors for coverage; when utility exhibits diminishing returns within near-duplicate groups, When </span><math id="S3.SS5.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\mathcal{S})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒮</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\mathcal{S})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is a monotone submodular coverage surrogate, standard submodular–knapsack
schemes achieve </span><math id="S3.SS5.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-1/e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-1/e)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-type approximations </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nemhauser et al., 1978</a>; <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Khuller et al., 1999</a>; <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sviridenko, 2004</a><span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.14" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Our default density-greedy by </span><math id="S3.SS5.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}=p_{i}/\ell_{i}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}=p_{i}/\ell_{i}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.15" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> instead optimizes
the </span><em id="S3.SS5.p1.1.16" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">modular</em><span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.17" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> sum </span><math id="S3.SS5.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\in\mathcal{S}}p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒮</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\in\mathcal{S}}p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.18" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and therefore does not inherit such guarantees;
we keep it for its simplicity and strong empirical performance.
. For in-context learning we select </span><em id="S3.SS5.p1.1.19" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">prompt packs</em><span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.20" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="S3.SS5.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi=\{(p_{i_{k}},r_{i_{k}})\}_{k=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi=\{(p_{i_{k}},r_{i_{k}})\}_{k=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.21" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> by maximizing summed prices under label/topic coverage and a maximum lexical-overlap constraint to avoid redundancy, realized by taking the top few </span><math id="S3.SS5.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.22" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> per label or reasoning type, enforcing at least one example per budgeted topic </span><math id="S3.SS5.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS5.p1.1.23" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and adding the next highest non-redundant item until the token budget is exhausted.</span></p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Maximum-entropy view with topic budgets.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let the topic masses </span><math id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\alpha_{t})_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\alpha_{t})_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> satisfy </span><math id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{t}\alpha_{t}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{t}\alpha_{t}=1</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
For each topic </span><math id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and signal </span><math id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, let </span><math id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{s}_{t}^{(m)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">¯</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{s}_{t}^{(m)}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> be given target (unnormalized)
moments, e.g. </span><math id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{s}_{t}^{(m)}=\alpha_{t}\,\mu_{t}^{(m)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">¯</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{s}_{t}^{(m)}=\alpha_{t}\,\mu_{t}^{(m)}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for desired topic-conditional
means </span><math id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu_{t}^{(m)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">μ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu_{t}^{(m)}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Consider</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{\pi\in\Delta^{N-1}}\;-\sum_{i=1}^{N}\pi_{i}\log\pi_{i}\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\sum_{j\in I_{t}}\pi_{j}=\alpha_{t},\ \ \sum_{j\in I_{t}}\pi_{j}\,s_{j}^{(m)}=\bar{s}_{t}^{(m)}\ \ \forall t,m." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">max</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.280em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><munderover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s.t.</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="1.000em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">¯</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{\pi\in\Delta^{N-1}}\;-\sum_{i=1}^{N}\pi_{i}\log\pi_{i}\quad\text{s.t.}\quad\sum_{j\in I_{t}}\pi_{j}=\alpha_{t},\ \ \sum_{j\in I_{t}}\pi_{j}\,s_{j}^{(m)}=\bar{s}_{t}^{(m)}\ \ \forall t,m.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">By convex duality (strict concavity of entropy and linear constraints),
the optimizer is unique (if feasible) and has the form</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{i}\;=\;\alpha_{t(i)}\;\frac{\exp\!\big(\sum_{m}\lambda_{t(i),m}\,s_{i}^{(m)}\big)}{\displaystyle\sum_{j\in I_{t(i)}}\exp\!\big(\sum_{m}\lambda_{t(i),m}\,s_{j}^{(m)}\big)}\;=\;\alpha_{t(i)}\,\Big[\mathrm{softmax}_{I_{t(i)}}\!\big(\sum_{m}\lambda_{t(i),m}\,s^{(m)}\big)\Big]_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.558em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.558em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">softmax</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{i}\;=\;\alpha_{t(i)}\;\frac{\exp\!\big(\sum_{m}\lambda_{t(i),m}\,s_{i}^{(m)}\big)}{\displaystyle\sum_{j\in I_{t(i)}}\exp\!\big(\sum_{m}\lambda_{t(i),m}\,s_{j}^{(m)}\big)}\;=\;\alpha_{t(i)}\,\Big[\mathrm{softmax}_{I_{t(i)}}\!\big(\sum_{m}\lambda_{t(i),m}\,s^{(m)}\big)\Big]_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">When the signals are the normalized </span><math id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{s}^{(m)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{s}^{(m)}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> used in our model and the
prices follow Eqs. (</span><a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2.4 Topic-separable markets for prompts ‣ 2 Problem formulation and method ‣ Market-Based Data Subset Selection - Principled Aggregation of Multi-Criteria Example Utility" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a><span id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.3.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)-(</span><a href="#S2.E5" title="In 2.4 Topic-separable markets for prompts ‣ 2 Problem formulation and method ‣ Market-Based Data Subset Selection - Principled Aggregation of Multi-Criteria Example Utility" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a><span id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.3.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">), this matches the LMSR form with the identification</span></p>
<table id="S3.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{t,m}\;=\;\frac{w_{m}}{\beta_{t}}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">λ</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.558em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.558em">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.170em" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{t,m}\;=\;\frac{w_{m}}{\beta_{t}}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">so Eq. (</span><a href="#S2.E5" title="In 2.4 Topic-separable markets for prompts ‣ 2 Problem formulation and method ‣ Market-Based Data Subset Selection - Principled Aggregation of Multi-Criteria Example Utility" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a><span id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.4.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) (and its cost Eq. (</span><a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2.4 Topic-separable markets for prompts ‣ 2 Problem formulation and method ‣ Market-Based Data Subset Selection - Principled Aggregation of Multi-Criteria Example Utility" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a><span id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.4.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)) realizes the
</span><em id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.4.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">unique</em><span id="S3.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.4.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> maximum-entropy distribution that is consistent with the topic masses
and the specified signal moments, while remaining agnostic beyond those constraints.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.6 </span>Practical considerations for prompt signals</h3>

<div id="S3.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS6.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">All signals are prompt-native, difficulty is the mean token-level NLL/perplexity of the reference response; optional gradient-style proxies use a linear probe on frozen instruction embeddings with predictive margin times embedding norm; </span><math id="S3.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS6.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">NN anti-density uses cosine distance in instruction space; diversity relative to centroids follows after clustering prompts by topic or reasoning pattern. Two adjustments are essential in the LLM regime difficulty signals are length-normalized to avoid rewarding verbosity, and standardization is performed </span><em id="S3.SS6.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">within topic</em><span id="S3.SS6.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> so high-volume topics do not saturate prices at small kept-rates after which the multi-signal LMSR in Eq. (</span><a href="#S2.E3" title="In 2.2 Aggregating heterogeneous signals ‣ 2 Problem formulation and method ‣ Market-Based Data Subset Selection - Principled Aggregation of Multi-Criteria Example Utility" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a><span id="S3.SS6.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) and the token-budgeted selector in Section </span><a href="#S3.SS5" title="3.5 Token-budgeted selection and prompt packs ‣ 3 Theoretical analysis ‣ Market-Based Data Subset Selection - Principled Aggregation of Multi-Criteria Example Utility" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a><span id="S3.SS6.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> apply verbatim.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.7 </span>LLM-specific utilities and guarantees</h3>

<div id="S3.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Utility for prompts is measured by downstream reward after a small fine-tuning step or by in-context performance at a fixed shot count; under the same monotonicity and noise assumptions as Proposition </span><a href="#S3.SS2" title="3.2 Utility recovery under noisy signals ‣ 3 Theoretical analysis ‣ Market-Based Data Subset Selection - Principled Aggregation of Multi-Criteria Example Utility" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a><span id="S3.SS7.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, now applied to length-normalized, topic-wise </span><math id="S3.SS7.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS7.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-scored signals, selection by market prices achieves near-optimal token-budgeted utility up to an error that shrinks with budget. In particular, if the aggregate prompt signal maintains a fixed signal-to-noise gap with respect to true reward and paraphrase perturbations induce sub-Gaussian score fluctuations, then the greedy price-per-token rule with topic floors is a practical heuristic that performed well
empirically in our settings (but we do not claim a formal approximation guarantee for this rule) with topic floors recovers at least </span><math id="S3.SS7.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϵ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS7.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> of the optimal budget-</span><math id="S3.SS7.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS7.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> reward with probability </span><math id="S3.SS7.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS7.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, with </span><math id="S3.SS7.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon=O(\sqrt{\log(N/\delta)/(B\,\gamma^{2})})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ϵ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon=O(\sqrt{\log(N/\delta)/(B\,\gamma^{2})})</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS7.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> after converting </span><math id="S3.SS7.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS7.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> to an effective number of average-length items, matching the qualitative guarantees of fixed-length, item-cost–agnostic settings while explicitly accounting for tokenized costs.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS8" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.8 </span>Evaluation protocols and market supervision</h3>

<div id="S3.SS8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Our selector is the same across tasks, signals are standardized within topic, aggregated into shares,
and priced by the topic-separable LMSR; subsets are then produced either by a balanced top-</span><math id="S3.SS8.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS8.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> head
(with minimal per-topic floors) or by the token-budgeted greedy head using </span><math id="S3.SS8.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}=p_{i}/\ell_{i}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}=p_{i}/\ell_{i}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS8.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
Unless noted we use </span><math id="S3.SS8.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}\propto|I_{t}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∝</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}\propto|I_{t}|</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS8.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, a single liquidity </span><math id="S3.SS8.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS8.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, and </span><math id="S3.SS8.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=1.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=1.6</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.SS8.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Experiments</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We evaluate the market-based selector in language reasoning under strict token budgets, using matched compute and identical fine-tuning hyperparameters across selectors. Unless noted, we report mean</span><math id="S4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">std over 3 random seeds.</span></p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Prompt-level selection for reasoning (GSM8K) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cobbe et al., 2021</a>)</cite></h4>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We treat each training item as a </span><em id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">prompt</em><span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="z_{i}=(p_{i},r_{i},\ell_{i},t(i))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">z</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">z_{i}=(p_{i},r_{i},\ell_{i},t(i))</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> with instruction </span><math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, target response </span><math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, token cost </span><math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (prompt</span><math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">response length), and topic </span><math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t(i)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t(i)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Prices are computed by a topic-separable LMSR (Section </span><a href="#S2.SS4" title="2.4 Topic-separable markets for prompts ‣ 2 Problem formulation and method ‣ Market-Based Data Subset Selection - Principled Aggregation of Multi-Criteria Example Utility" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a><span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">): signals are standardized within topic, priced with liquidity </span><math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, then normalized across topics using topic budgets. Unless stated, we use the degenerate choice </span><math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{t}\propto|\mathcal{I}_{t}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∝</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℐ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{t}\propto|\mathcal{I}_{t}|</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and a single global liquidity </span><math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.13" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Setup.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We format GSM8K examples as </span><span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">‘‘Question: … Answer:’’</span><span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and count tokens over prompt</span><math id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="+" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">+</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">gold answer for the budget. All selectors use the same backbone and optimizer; selection signals include token-level NLL and embedding rarity, with optional diversity. We evaluate at a fixed 60k-token budget. We follow standard practice for GSM8K </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cobbe et al., 2021</a><span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="S4.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 1: </span>Performance comparison against algorithmic baselines across different training configurations. Results averaged over 3 seeds with standard deviations.</figcaption>
<div id="S4.T1.4" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:397.5pt;height:156pt;vertical-align:-76.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-48.8pt,19.2pt) scale(0.80273992383985,0.80273992383985) ;">
<table id="S4.T1.4.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S4.T1.4.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T1.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Configuration</span></th>
<th id="S4.T1.4.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T1.4.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Method</span></th>
<th id="S4.T1.4.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T1.4.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Eval Loss</span><span id="S4.T1.4.1.1.3.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="S4.T1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="S4.T1.4.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T1.4.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Exact Match</span><span id="S4.T1.4.1.1.4.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><math id="S4.T1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<th id="S4.T1.4.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T1.4.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Median Tokens</span></th>
<th id="S4.T1.4.1.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T1.4.1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">N Selected</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
