<div id="p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Appendix<span id="p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text"></span></span></p>
</div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Method Details (LMSR, Topic-Separable Pricing)</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We use the temperature/liquidity convention for LMSR. For shares </span><math id="A1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in\mathbb{R}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in\mathbb{R}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and per-topic partitions </span><math id="A1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{I_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{I_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> with budgets </span><math id="A1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\alpha_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\alpha_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and liquidities </span><math id="A1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\beta_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\beta_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">,</span></p>
<table id="A1.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(q)=\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\alpha_{t}\,\beta_{t}\log\!\Big(\sum_{j\in I_{t}}e^{\,q_{j}/\beta_{t}}\Big),\qquad p_{i}=\alpha_{t(i)}\Big[\mathrm{softmax}_{I_{t(i)}}\!\big(q/\beta_{t(i)}\big)\Big]_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒯</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow></munder><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">softmax</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(q)=\sum_{t\in\mathcal{T}}\alpha_{t}\,\beta_{t}\log\!\Big(\sum_{j\in I_{t}}e^{\,q_{j}/\beta_{t}}\Big),\qquad p_{i}=\alpha_{t(i)}\Big[\mathrm{softmax}_{I_{t(i)}}\!\big(q/\beta_{t(i)}\big)\Big]_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(A.1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">As </span><math id="A1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}\to 0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="A1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(q)\to\sum_{t}\alpha_{t}\max_{j\in I_{t}}q_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">max</mi><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">I</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(q)\to\sum_{t}\alpha_{t}\max_{j\in I_{t}}q_{j}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.p1.2.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">; as </span><math id="A1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{t}\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{t}\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, prices become uniform within topic </span><math id="A1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
This follows the cost-function market view of LMSR and its convexity/elicitation properties </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="A1.p1.2.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hanson, 2007</a>; <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Abernethy et al., 2013</a>; <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chen &amp; Vaughan, 2010</a>; <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lambert et al., 2008</a><span id="A1.p1.2.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="A1.p1.2.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
Signals are standardized within topic (z-score or rank to </span><math id="A1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.p1.2.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">), mixed as </span><math id="A1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}=\sum_{k}w_{k}\,\tilde{s}_{i}^{(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}=\sum_{k}w_{k}\,\tilde{s}_{i}^{(k)}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.p1.2.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, priced per topic, then converted to a decision.</span></p>
</div>
<section id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Decision heads.</h4>

<div id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(i) </span><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Balanced top-<math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>:</span><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> apply minimal per-topic floors before filling by global price. (ii) </span><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Token-budget greedy:</span><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> score </span><math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}=p_{i}/\ell_{i}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}=p_{i}/\ell_{i}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and admit by descending </span><math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> under </span><math id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\in\mathcal{R}}\ell_{i}\leq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">ℛ</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\in\mathcal{R}}\ell_{i}\leq B</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. For coverage-like utilities, greedy enjoys classical constant-factor behavior under a knapsack constraint </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nemhauser et al., 1978</a>; <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Sviridenko, 2004</a>; <a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">Khuller et al., 1999</a>; <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wei et al., 2015</a>; <a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lin &amp; Bilmes, 2011</a><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="A1.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.12" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Recovery Guarantees and Cost-Aware Greedy</h2>

<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Setup.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let </span><math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U=(U_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\in[0,1]^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U=(U_{i})_{i=1}^{N}\in[0,1]^{N}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> denote unknown utilities.
Signals are standardized within topic and mixed as
</span><math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}=\sum_{m=1}^{M}w_{m}\tilde{s}_{i}^{(m)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">M</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">~</mo></mover><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}=\sum_{m=1}^{M}w_{m}\tilde{s}_{i}^{(m)}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">; prices are
</span><math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\beta}=\mathrm{softmax}(q/\beta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">softmax</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\beta}=\mathrm{softmax}(q/\beta)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> as in Eqs. </span><a href="#S2.E3" title="In 2.2 Aggregating heterogeneous signals ‣ 2 Problem formulation and method ‣ Market-Based Data Subset Selection - Principled Aggregation of Multi-Criteria Example Utility" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.3</span></a><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
Selecting top-</span><math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> by </span><math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is equivalent to selecting top-</span><math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> by </span><math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.9" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (softmax is order-preserving).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmassumption1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmassumption1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmassumption1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Monotone alignment with margin)<span id="A2.Thmassumption1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">There exists a strictly increasing </span><math id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:[0,1]\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.278em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:[0,1]\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and a margin </span><math id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta_{K}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta_{K}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> such that
</span><math id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g(U_{(K)})-g(U_{(K+1)})\geq\Delta_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g(U_{(K)})-g(U_{(K+1)})\geq\Delta_{K}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, where </span><math id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="U_{(1)}\geq\cdots\geq U_{(N)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.1389em">≥</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.1389em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.1389em">⋯</mo><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.1389em" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">U_{(1)}\geq\cdots\geq U_{(N)}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and
</span><math id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T^{\star}=\{(1),\ldots,(K)\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⋆</mo></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T^{\star}=\{(1),\ldots,(K)\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.Thmassumption1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmassumption2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_assumption">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmassumption2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Assumption B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmassumption2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Sub-Gaussian noise)<span id="A2.Thmassumption2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmassumption2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmassumption2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A2.Thmassumption2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{i}=g(U_{i})+\xi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ξ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{i}=g(U_{i})+\xi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.Thmassumption2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> with independent mean-zero </span><math id="A2.Thmassumption2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.Thmassumption2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-sub-Gaussian </span><math id="A2.Thmassumption2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ξ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.Thmassumption2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
Define </span><math id="A2.Thmassumption2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Gamma_{K}:=\Delta_{K}/\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Gamma_{K}:=\Delta_{K}/\sigma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.Thmassumption2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Top-<math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> recovery up to a small utility gap)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{T}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{T}</annotation></semantics></math> be the top-<math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\beta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\beta}</annotation></semantics></math> (equivalently by <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math>).
Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> be a Lipschitz constant of <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math>.
With probability at least <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{K}\sum_{i\in T^{\star}}U_{i}\;-\;\frac{1}{K}\sum_{i\in\widehat{T}}U_{i}\;\leq\;\frac{2L}{K}\cdot\frac{\sigma}{\Delta_{K}}\sqrt{2\log\!\Big(\frac{2N^{2}}{\delta}\Big)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⋆</mo></msup></mrow></munder><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.502em">−</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover></mrow></munder><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">U</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.558em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.146em;" width="1.146em"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{K}\sum_{i\in T^{\star}}U_{i}\;-\;\frac{1}{K}\sum_{i\in\widehat{T}}U_{i}\;\leq\;\frac{2L}{K}\cdot\frac{\sigma}{\Delta_{K}}\sqrt{2\log\!\Big(\frac{2N^{2}}{\delta}\Big)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">In particular, the shortfall is
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\!\big(\Gamma_{K}^{-1}\sqrt{\tfrac{\log(N/\delta)}{K}}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\!\big(\Gamma_{K}^{-1}\sqrt{\tfrac{\log(N/\delta)}{K}}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\in T^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\in T^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j\notin T^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∉</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">T</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⋆</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j\notin T^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[q_{i}-q_{j}]\geq\Delta_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[q_{i}-q_{j}]\geq\Delta_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi_{j}-\xi_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ξ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ξ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi_{j}-\xi_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-sub-Gaussian, so
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[q_{i}&lt;q_{j}]\leq e^{-\Gamma_{K}^{2}/4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Pr</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">j</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[q_{i}&lt;q_{j}]\leq e^{-\Gamma_{K}^{2}/4}</annotation></semantics></math>.
A union bound at the top-<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> boundary implies that, with prob. <math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>,
the number of boundary inversions is at most
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{2\sigma}{\Delta_{K}}\sqrt{2\log(2N^{2}/\delta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi></mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{2\sigma}{\Delta_{K}}\sqrt{2\log(2N^{2}/\delta)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Each such inversion changes the average utility by at most
<math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{L}{K}\cdot\tfrac{2\sigma}{\Delta_{K}}\sqrt{2\log(2N^{2}/\delta)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">L</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">σ</mi></mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{L}{K}\cdot\tfrac{2\sigma}{\Delta_{K}}\sqrt{2\log(2N^{2}/\delta)}</annotation></semantics></math>,
yielding the bound. Order preservation of softmax completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Topic-separable markets.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Within each topic, prices follow Eq. </span><a href="#S2.E5" title="In 2.4 Topic-separable markets for prompts ‣ 2 Problem formulation and method ‣ Market-Based Data Subset Selection - Principled Aggregation of Multi-Criteria Example Utility" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, which is order-preserving in </span><math id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.
Thus Theorem </span><a href="#A2.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem B.1 (Top-𝐾 recovery up to a small utility gap). ‣ Setup. ‣ Appendix B Recovery Guarantees and Cost-Aware Greedy ‣ Market-Based Data Subset Selection - Principled Aggregation of Multi-Criteria Example Utility" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> applies per topic (Eqs. </span><a href="#S2.E4" title="In 2.4 Topic-separable markets for prompts ‣ 2 Problem formulation and method ‣ Market-Based Data Subset Selection - Principled Aggregation of Multi-Criteria Example Utility" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.4</span></a><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">–</span><a href="#S2.E5" title="In 2.4 Topic-separable markets for prompts ‣ 2 Problem formulation and method ‣ Market-Based Data Subset Selection - Principled Aggregation of Multi-Criteria Example Utility" class="ltx_ref" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.5</span></a><span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">) and to the merged list.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SSx1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Cost-aware selection and <math id="A2.SSx1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>-greedy</h3>

<div id="A2.SSx1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SSx1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SSx1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We select under token costs </span><math id="A2.SSx1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.SSx1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> with budget </span><math id="A2.SSx1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.SSx1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> by ranking
</span><math id="A2.SSx1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}=p_{i}/\ell_{i}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}=p_{i}/\ell_{i}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.SSx1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and greedy filling.
This optimizes a modular objective under a knapsack constraint
and thus </span><em id="A2.SSx1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">does not</em><span id="A2.SSx1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> inherit </span><math id="A2.SSx1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-1/e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-1/e)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.SSx1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> guarantees available for
submodular objectives.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Greedy-or-best-single: a <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1/2</annotation></semantics></math>-approximation)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}:=\ell_{i}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">:=</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}:=\ell_{i}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math> and consider the 0–1 knapsack
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\max_{S}\sum_{i\in S}p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow><mprescripts></mprescripts><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\max_{S}\sum_{i\in S}p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> s.t. <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\in S}c_{i}\leq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">S</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\in S}c_{i}\leq B</annotation></semantics></math>.
Take the better of:
(i) density-greedy by <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}/c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}/c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
(ii) the single best item that fits.
This achieves value at least <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tfrac{1}{2}\,\mathrm{OPT}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">OPT</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tfrac{1}{2}\,\mathrm{OPT}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SSx1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Proof sketch.</h6>
<div id="A2.SSx1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SSx1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SSx1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The fractional relaxation is solved by ratio greedy.
Rounding either returns the greedy set or the last fractional item alone.
One of these has value <math id="A2.SSx1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> of the fractional optimum,
which upper-bounds the integral optimum.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Near-optimal token utility under mild length dispersion)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">If <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell_{i}\in[\underline{\ell},\overline{\ell}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><munder accentunder="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell_{i}\in[\underline{\ell},\overline{\ell}]</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\overline{\ell}/\underline{\ell}\leq C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><munder accentunder="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></munder></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\overline{\ell}/\underline{\ell}\leq C</annotation></semantics></math>,
write <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{\mathrm{eff}}:=\lfloor B/\overline{\ell}\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">eff</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">:=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="true">¯</mo></mover></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{\mathrm{eff}}:=\lfloor B/\overline{\ell}\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under Assumptions 1–2, the <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>-greedy selection
(with <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in[1,2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in[1,2]</annotation></semantics></math>) attains token-normalized utility within
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O\!\big(\Gamma_{K_{\mathrm{eff}}}^{-1}\sqrt{\tfrac{\log(N/\delta)}{K_{\mathrm{eff}}}}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.621em;" width="0.621em"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Γ</mi><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">eff</mi></msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">eff</mi></msub></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O\!\big(\Gamma_{K_{\mathrm{eff}}}^{-1}\sqrt{\tfrac{\log(N/\delta)}{K_{\mathrm{eff}}}}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>
of the budgeted optimum with probability <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\geq 1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\geq 1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SSx1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SSx1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SSx1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Practical note.</span><span id="A2.SSx1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> When coverage-style utilities are used (e.g., facility location),
classical submodular-knapsack schemes provide </span><math id="A2.SSx1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-1/e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-1/e)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.SSx1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-type guarantees; our default
</span><math id="A2.SSx1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A2.SSx1.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">-greedy targets the modular sum and is kept for its simplicity and speed.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Diagnostics &amp; Metrics</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We report subset shape with three simple diagnostics.</span></p>
<ul id="A3.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Balance score:</span><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for empirical topic mass </span><math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\pi}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\pi}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and target </span><math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{BalScore}=\frac{1}{2}\|\hat{\pi}-\alpha\|_{1}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">BalScore</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">π</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">^</mo></mover><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">α</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{BalScore}=\frac{1}{2}\|\hat{\pi}-\alpha\|_{1}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> (lower is more balanced).</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Normalized effective sample size (nESS):</span><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for counts </span><math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{n_{t}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{n_{t}\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N=\sum_{t}n_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∑</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N=\sum_{t}n_{t}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ESS}=\frac{N^{2}}{\sum_{t}n_{t}^{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ESS</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi></msub></mstyle><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">t</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ESS}=\frac{N^{2}}{\sum_{t}n_{t}^{2}}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{nESS}=\mathrm{ESS}/|\mathcal{T}|\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">nESS</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ESS</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathcolor="#000000">𝒯</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{nESS}=\mathrm{ESS}/|\mathcal{T}|\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Rarity coverage:</span><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> with kNN anti-density </span><math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">r</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">, </span><math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Rare@q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">Rare</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">@</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Rare@q}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is the fraction of selected items in the top-</span><math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">th rarity percentile.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">These relate to coverage-style objectives used in summarization/data selection </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="A3.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lin &amp; Bilmes, 2011</a>; <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wei et al., 2015</a><span id="A3.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="A3.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Calibration &amp; Hyperparameters</h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We expose three knobs and tune them deterministically on a tiny dev split.</span></p>
<ol id="A4.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Liquidity <math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>:</span><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> binary-search to hit a target price entropy band or desired nESS (large </span><math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> smoother; small </span><math id="A4.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> sharper) </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hanson, 2007</a>; <a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Abernethy et al., 2013</a><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="A4.I1.i1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Signal weights <math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>:</span><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> default </span><math id="A4.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{k}=1/K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">w</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{k}=1/K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">; optionally apply a single Exponentiated-Gradient pass on a small grid </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Arora et al., 2012</a><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="A4.I1.i2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Length bias <math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>:</span><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for token budgets only; choose </span><math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\in\{1.4,1.6,1.8\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∈</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1.4</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1.6</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1.8</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\in\{1.4,1.6,1.8\}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> by compute profile (larger </span><math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> favors many short items; smaller </span><math id="A4.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A4.I1.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> favors fewer long items).</span></p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="A4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">ANN backends (FAISS/HNSW) are used for diversity/rarity when enabled </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="A4.p1.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Johnson et al., 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Malkov &amp; Yashunin, 2020</a><span id="A4.p1.2.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="A4.p1.2.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Complexity &amp; Scaling</h2>

<div id="A5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Standardization and mixing are </span><math id="A5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(NK)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(NK)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">; topic-separable LMSR pricing is </span><math id="A5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">; token-budget greedy is one sort </span><math id="A5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N\log N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N\log N)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> plus a linear scan. Optional ANN kNN uses an </span><math id="A5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N\log N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N\log N)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> index build and sublinear queries in practice. Memory is </span><math id="A5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(Nd)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">d</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(Nd)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for embeddings plus </span><math id="A5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O(N)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">N</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O(N)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> for prices/shares. Selection overhead is negligible relative to fine-tuning in our runs.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix F </span>Experimental Details</h2>

<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Backbone and tooling.</h4>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We keep optimizer, steps, batch size, and initialization identical across selectors. Code relies on </span><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">transformers</span><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">/</span><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">datasets</span><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> and </span><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">sentence-transformers</span><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.7" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.8" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib29" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wolf et al., 2020</a>; <a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lhoest et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">Reimers &amp; Gurevych, 2019</a><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.10" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.11" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Seeds are fixed for data order and initialization.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">GSM8K (reasoning) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Cobbe et al., 2021</a>)</cite>.</h4>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Format: </span><code id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_verbatim ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Question: ... Answer:</code><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">. Budget: 60k tokens over selected items (prompt+gold under the model tokenizer). Signals: length-normalized token-level NLL (uncertainty) and embedding-space rarity; optional lightweight diversity head where noted. Metrics: validation loss and exact match (mean</span><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">std over seeds). Decision: token-budget greedy with </span><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}=p_{i}/\ell_{i}^{\gamma}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">ρ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">p</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><msubsup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">i</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}=p_{i}/\ell_{i}^{\gamma}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">; default </span><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=1.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=1.6</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">AGNews (classification) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib30" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zhang et al., 2015</a>)</cite>.</h4>

<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Format: instruction–label pairs. Budgets: fixed kept-rates (</span><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">kept</span><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">={5,10,25}%). Metrics: accuracy (mean</span><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pm" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">±</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pm</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">std). Decision: cardinality (no token costs), using either balanced top-</span><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> with minimal per-topic floors or unbalanced global top-</span><math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> by price. We also report BalScore to summarize coverage when floors are active.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A7" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix G </span>Ablations (Qualitative)</h2>

<div id="A7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">We summarize ablation tendencies without plots (reproducible via code).</span></p>
<ul id="A7.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A7.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Liquidity <math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>:</span><span id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> increasing </span><math id="A7.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.i1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> raises price entropy and nESS (smoother markets), reducing over-concentration on any single signal.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Diversity head:</span><span id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> improves Rare@q and coverage with a small change in loss; most helpful when pools contain near-duplicates </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lin &amp; Bilmes, 2011</a>; <a href="#bib.bib28" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wei et al., 2015</a><span id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="A7.I1.i2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div></li>
<li id="A7.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A7.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A7.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Length bias <math id="A7.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>:</span><span id="A7.I1.i3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> larger </span><math id="A7.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.i3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> shifts selection toward many short prompts (higher item count, lower median length); smaller </span><math id="A7.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.i3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> admits fewer long prompts. Accuracy remains within noise across practical settings; </span><math id="A7.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A7.I1.i3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> is a curriculum-style knob.</span></p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A8" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix H </span>Broader Impact and Limitations</h2>

<div id="A8.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A8.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A8.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Data selection can reduce compute and energy by focusing training on informative items, but it also shapes topic/population coverage. Our topic budgets and balance diagnostics make such choices explicit. Limitations include sensitivity at very aggressive budgets, robustness to misspecified signals (mitigated by clipping and within-topic standardization), and the need for re-calibration on multi-modal or cross-lingual corpora. Diversity kNN can be heavier at scale; we therefore use approximate search backends </span><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep"><span id="A8.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">(</span><a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Johnson et al., 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Malkov &amp; Yashunin, 2020</a><span id="A8.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">)</span></cite><span id="A8.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">.</span></p>
</div>
</section>
</article>
</div>
</div>
